Goals
=====

- Writing BTF from scratch.
- Extending an existing BTF.
- Merging BTF and 1-n splits BTF. Allows extending a split BTF using 3 then 2.
  => Would allow attaching a unified BTF representation to BPF programs and
     use BTF ids to allow handling all types at runtime.

API
===

Use an optional base `Btf` as a ref, write new data to internal maps.

- A dedicated `BtfBuilder`:
  + `BtfBuilder::new()`
  + `BtfBuilder::from_btf(&Btf)`

- `BtfBuilder::add_string(&mut self, s: String) -> Result<u32>`.

- `BtfBuilder::add_type(&mut self, ty: Type) -> Result<u32>`.

- `BtfBuilder::merge_split_btf(&mut self, &Btf) -> Result<()>` — Merges
  `Btf::split()` aka. get all its strings and types and write them as if it
  were new data. `BtfBuilder::merge_btf(&mut self, &Btf) -> Result<()>` to also
  allow merging `Btf::base()`?

- `BtfBuilder::to_btf(&self) -> Result<Btf>`. How to cover a split base `Btf`?

- `BtfBuilder::write(&self, &mut Write)` — issue the full representation.

- `BtfBuilder::write_split(&self, &mut Write)` — issue the split (added
  strings / types) only.

- Move `Btf` API into a trait and implement it there too => required to get
  type and strings ids and be able to reference them. Should `BtfBuilder` be
  `Btf` directly?

- Use a `CachedBtfSection` internally for new strings and types?
  + Can implement strings / types writing ops itself.
  + Can share a write op trait with `MmapBtfSection` to write raw BTF data,
    allowing to not rely on getters and making the mmap backend just a raw copy
    of the full data.

Deduplication
=============

- Str dedup: only insert after failed lookup should already the base `Btf` +
  added strings map.
  + Lookup; should already cover the base + added strings.
  + Reuse offset if there's a match.
  + Otherwise insert new string.

- Types dedup:
  + Lookup by name; should already cover the base + added types + anon types.
  + Compare returned `Type`. Reuse id if match.
  + Otherwise insert new type.
